# ── Frontend (Vite) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From Supabase project settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

# ── Supabase Edge Functions ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these with: supabase secrets set KEY=value
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected automatically
# by the platform for every deployed function — you do NOT set them
# yourself, they're listed here only so you know they exist.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=(automatic)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=(automatic)

# Restrict CORS on the edge functions to your real frontend origin(s).
# Comma-separate if you have more than one (e.g. staging + prod) and
# adjust _shared/helpers.ts's corsHeaders to check against a list instead
# of a single value if you do.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://app.seba.example

# WebAuthn / passkeys — MUST match your real deployed domain and origin
# exactly or every passkey registration/login will fail verification.
# For local dev this can stay as localhost.
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=app.seba.example
WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=https://app.seba.example

# ── OAuth (Google / Apple) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Configured in the Supabase dashboard under Authentication → Providers,
# not as env vars here — see README "Social login" section for the
# checklist of what each provider needs.
